course: dictionary
lesson: 6651
title: Numbness: not being able to feel
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Numbness is a noun, a thing you can have. It means you cannot feel something in a part of your body, like your lip after the dentist's injection. «A filling repairs a hole in a tooth; the dentist numbs the area first.» The numbness is the missing feeling, so the area feels nothing at all for a while.
explain: Numbness can also be about feelings. «Numbness, feeling nothing at all, is a common first reaction to a shock or a death.» Here the word means that a person feels nothing inside for a time, often after bad news. The context tells you the person is in shock, not that they do not care.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like dentist, fingers or cold point to the body meaning. Words like shock, death or bad news point to the feelings meaning. Then try your meaning in the sentence: if "a person felt nothing at all" fits, you have it right.
fact: Numbness means not being able to feel something.
fact: Numbness in the body can come from cold, pressure or an injection, because these stop nerves sending messages.
fact: Numbness can also mean feeling no emotions for a while, often after shock or sad news.
fact: Sudden numbness can be a sign to get help quickly, so tell an adult straight away.
fact: Useful phrases: "numbness in my fingers" and "a feeling of numbness".
exercise: After the dentist's injection, my lip had numbness. What does numbness mean? | Feeling very cold all over | Feeling a great deal of pain | Feeling sleepy in class | *Not being able to feel my lip
exercise: «Numbness, feeling nothing at all, is a common first reaction to a shock.» What does numbness mean here? | Feeling extremely excited | *Feeling nothing for a while after a shock | A sign of a good friend | Shouting loudly straight away
exercise: Which clue in «Numbness, feeling nothing at all, is a common first reaction to a shock or a death» shows the feelings meaning? | fingers | cold | *shock | dentist
test: «The numbness lasts a couple of hours, so talking and eating are hard.» What does numbness mean in this sentence? | Feeling very hungry | Feeling sad about a friend | *Not being able to feel part of your mouth | A loud noise
test: Which sentence uses numbness to mean feeling nothing after shock? | My toes had numbness from the snow. | The numbness of the bus made me sleepy. | *After the terrible news, she sat in numbness for an hour. | I had numbness in my hand after the injection.
exam: Why does the author add «it does not mean the person didn't care» after numbness? | To tell readers numbness is always caused by cold | To make the sentence longer | To show numbness is a kind of happiness | *To stop readers thinking numbness means someone is uncaring
